## 1. What landed: the missing pin (2 new `deftest`s + 3 private helpers)

`test/yang/clojure_test.clj`, one file only.

**Why these pins:** every committed R3 pin (`test-exception-r3-protocol-condition-forwarded-unchanged`, `test-exception-r3-astra-probes`, `test-exception-r3-condition-field-preserved`) drives `run-cell-program`/`run-library`, i.e. `(receive marker-operand)` where `receive` is a top-level `defn` → `intra-unit-fn?` (`clojure.cljc:1556`) → `dsg__intra_call` **private token lane** → the retained wrapper is decoded by `strip-top-outcome` (`clojure.cljc:2560-2585`) at the harness top. The kit never goes near that site: `exception_probes.clj`'s `boundary-call-form` calls `yang.call/invoke` on the **published descriptor** read via `clj/global-get`, so classification is decided by `call-entry`'s **public** lane, `entry-body` (`clojure.cljc:1395-1414`). That is the uncovered path, and it is the only site in the whole clojure lane that can emit the observed `:yang.call/thrown`.

- `run-public-entry-program` — `run-cell-program` plus a spliced raw `u/lam` identity raise at `marker-raise`, so the call crosses the public entry and the answered value **is** the condition the entry handed the raise exit. (A guest `(fn [c] c)` will not do: under the outcome model it compiles to a descriptor map and `yang.call/invoke` refuses it `:missing-raise-exit`.)
- `test-exception-r3-protocol-condition-crosses-the-public-entry` — all three qualified reasons × immediate rethrow (`receive`) and saved/later rethrow (`retain` + `later`), both lanes, asserting `[:yin.k/ok condition]`, i.e. qualified reason **and** condition identity. This is `:clojure/protocol-*` and `:clojure/saved-protocol-*` at unit scale.
- `uast-variable-names` / `uast-global-reads` + `test-exception-r3-linked-unit-keeps-the-retained-seam` — pins the one transformation the kit applies and no local pin does: `lower-unit` → `publish-to-globals` (`clojure.cljc:3402-3444`). Asserts `cell/dsg__new-retained` and `cell/retained?` survive as host reads and that no qualified or `dsg__`-prefixed name was rewritten into a `clj/global-get` lookup.

```diff
--- a/test/yang/clojure_test.clj
+++ b/test/yang/clojure_test.clj
@@ -1464,6 +1464,7 @@
 (declare run-cell-program)
+(declare run-public-entry-program)
 (declare run-library library-opts)
@@ -1526,6 +1527,105 @@
+(deftest test-exception-r3-protocol-condition-crosses-the-public-entry
+  (testing "the acceptance kit's boundary shape: ... the PUBLIC entry ...
+            never re-minted as a fresh :yang.call/thrown. ..."
+    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]
+      (doseq [[reason evidence]
+              [[:yang.call/not-callable {:yang.call/callee {}}]
+               [:yang.call/invalid-invocation {:yang.call/callee :target}]
+               [:yang.call/unsupported-binding
+                {:yang.call/binding-profile :contract/unsupported}]]]
+        (let [condition {:yang.call/reason reason :yang.call/data evidence}]
+          (is (= [:yin.k/ok condition]
+                 (run-public-entry-program
+                   '[(defn receive [f] (try (f) (catch Exception e (throw e))))
+                     (yang.call/invoke receive (conj [] marker-operand) []
+                                       marker-raise)]
+                   (cell-entry-node condition) lane)) ...)))))
+  (testing "the saved variant: ... a LATER activation ..."
+    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]
+      (doseq [reason [:yang.call/not-callable :yang.call/invalid-invocation
+                      :yang.call/unsupported-binding]]
+        (let [condition {:yang.call/reason reason
+                         :yang.call/data {:yang.call/callee :target}}]
+          (is (= [:yin.k/ok condition]
+                 (run-public-entry-program
+                   '[(def saved (cell/new nil))
+                     (defn retain [f] (try (f) (catch Exception e (cell/set! saved e) e)))
+                     (defn later [] (throw (cell/get saved)))
+                     (let [_held (retain marker-operand)]
+                       (yang.call/invoke later (conj []) [] marker-raise))]
+                   (cell-entry-node condition) lane)) ...))))))
+
+(defn- uast-variable-names [node] ...)      ; every :variable name in a map AST
+(defn- uast-global-reads  [node] ...)      ; every clj/global-get key in a map AST
+
+(deftest test-exception-r3-linked-unit-keeps-the-retained-seam
+  (testing "a LINKED unit's wrapper helpers still read the issuer's retained
+            mint and query as host names. ..."
+    (let [unit    (yang/lower-unit (yang/read-forms "...receive/saved/retain/later...") [])
+          names   (uast-variable-names unit)
+          globals (uast-global-reads unit)]
+      (is (contains? names 'cell/dsg__new-retained) "...")
+      (is (contains? names 'cell/retained?) "...")
+      (is (empty? (filter #(or (some? (namespace (symbol %)))
+                               (.startsWith ^String % "dsg__")) globals)) "..."))))
@@ -2519,6 +2619,36 @@
+(defn- run-public-entry-program
+  "Like `run-cell-program`, but the call under test is an explicit
+   `yang.call/invoke` on the callee's published descriptor rather than an
+   intra-unit call, and the invocation's raise exit is a raw identity
+   lambda spliced at `marker-raise`. The condition therefore crosses
+   `call-entry`'s PUBLIC lane (`entry-body`) ..."
+  [program node lane]
+  (let [raise  (u/lam ['marker_condition] (u/v 'marker_condition))
+        splice (fn [n] (cond (and (map? n) (= :variable (:type n)))
+                             (case (:name n)
+                               marker-operand node
+                               marker-raise   raise
+                               n)
+                             :else n))
+        ast (walk/postwalk splice
+              (yang/compile-program (into (yang/library-for program) program)
+                                    true library-opts))]
+    (try (run-guest-ast ast library-modules lane 1000000)
+         (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e
+           [:thrown (select-keys (ex-data e) [:reason :effect])]))))
```

## 2. Diagnosis — the classification site, with file:line, and what is *ruled out*

The observed `:reason :yang.call/thrown` has exactly **one** possible emitter in the clojure lane: `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1404-1414`, `entry-body`'s `(raise (yang.call/thrown err-val))` arm — i.e. `(dsg__equal retained nil)` was **true**, so `dsg__condition_retained` answered nil at the public entry. (`yang.call/thrown` appears nowhere else in `clojure.cljc`; `strip-top-outcome:2576-2584` returns the outcome vector, it never raises.)

Answering the brief's "not reached, or classified before the protocol check?" — **neither**:

- **`condition->outcome`'s protocol arm IS reached and DOES fire.** Its test is `(dsg__equal (dsg__get condition :yang.call/reason) :yang.call/not-callable)` (`clojure.cljc:1637-1644`), evaluated on a condition built by `yang.call/condition`. `dsg__get`/`dsg__equal` are the *same* helpers `entry-body` uses for `:yang.call/positional`/`:yang.call/named` and that `cell-ref-shaped-node` (`:1585-1604`) uses for routing — and `:clojure/binding`, `fresh-named`, `fresh-closure`, `shape-return`, `shape-throw` are green, which is impossible if they misfire. So the else arm (`:1649-1651`, "a value without a qualified reason") cannot be what delivered these six.
- **The refusal arms are not the emitter either.** `refused` (`:1663-1672`) mints a wrapper around a *fresh* `:yang.call/not-callable`; had it fired and decoded, `:clojure/protocol-not-callable` would have reported reason `:yang.call/not-callable` with `:condition-identical false`. It reported `:yang.call/thrown`.
- **Cell-ref routing is not the emitter.** I checked this because the six red fixtures are exactly the six whose callee is a `(cell/new …)` cell-ref while every green clojure row's callee is a descriptor map — so `fresh-closure` does *not* prove cell-ref routing works. But `run-cell-program`'s `cell-entry-node` (`clojure_test.clj:1470-1478`) builds a byte-identical 3-key cell-ref and the local protocol pins are green, so `cell-ref-shaped-node` + `cell/authentic?` + `dsg__admitted?`'s cell-ref branch behave the same in both compositions. Had routing gone to `value-call`, `invoke-value`'s lookup arm would have refused with `{:yin.k/message "Lookup invocation requires one key…"}` and the *local* pins would fail too.

**So: the wrapper is minted (`clojure.cljc:1645-1648` → `condition-wrapper-form:943-946` → `cell/dsg__new-retained`), and `dsg__condition_retained` (`:949-969`) fails to decode it at the public entry in the linked composition while decoding it correctly at `strip-top-outcome` locally.** The two call sites are structurally identical; the difference is the composition, not the code shape. I verified statically and can rule out: lexical scoping of the `cond->>` helper chain (`:2780-2812` — `E_call-entry` is the argument of the `dsg__make_entry` `let1`, so it sits inside the `dsg__condition_retained` binding); `dsg__assoc`'s 3-pair ceiling (the descriptor is exactly 3 pairs); `library-for`-dependent `dsg__get`/`dsg__assoc` variants (the library defines `rest` only — not `get`, `assoc`, `conj`, `vec`, `=`); `check-callee-effect!` (`engine.cljc:2431-2455`, `declared` is a union and a nil profile passes); GC (glm's P13 already proved `sweep` keeps whole entries, and `heap-write:2457-2463` preserves the mark).

**What I could not rule out without executing**, and what the new pin discriminates on first run — the pin prints the actual value, and `:yang.call/value` is decisive:

| `:yang.call/value` in the failure output | mechanism | fix site |
|---|---|---|
| `{:type :cell-ref, :id …, :seal …}` | wrapper minted, `cell/retained?` answers false in the linked task | `engine.cljc:2820-2837` / `retained-ref?:355-365` (VM seam) |
| `{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/not-callable, …}` (the raw condition) | qualified arm never minted | `clojure.cljc:1637-1651` |
| `{:yin.k/message "Lookup invocation…"}` | cell-ref routing fell to `value-call` | `clojure.cljc:1746-1758` |

